{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Agency.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Agency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"machine moral agency machine moral agency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Agency.md","fileName":"Machine Moral Agency.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Machine Moral Agency","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Machine Moral Status]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Algorithmic Accountability","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Agency.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Agency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"machine moral agency machine moral agency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Agency.md","fileName":"Machine Moral Agency.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Machine Moral Agency","heading":"Machine Moral Agency","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Machine moral agency is the capacity attributed to an artificial system when its behavior can be assessed in moral terms. A weak account asks whether the system interacts with its environment, acts with some autonomy, and adapts its behavior. A stronger account requires understanding, intention, freedom, and the ability to answer for a choice.\n\nCurrent systems may satisfy functional criteria without meeting the stronger conditions for responsibility. Calling them agents can describe their causal role, but it should not transfer [[Algorithmic Accountability]] away from the people and institutions that design, deploy, and benefit from them.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Algorithmic Accountability","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Agency.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Agency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"machine moral agency machine moral agency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Machine Moral Agency.md","fileName":"Machine Moral Agency.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Machine Moral Agency","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiethics.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Algorithmic Accountability","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}